   "text": {
    "L1": "A place becomes sacred when people connect it with the divine, a saint, a teacher or an important event.",
    "L2": "That place may be a river, mountain, cave, lake, spring or forest—not only a building.",
    "L3": "People remember the meaning of a place, visit it and care for it. Sacred groves can protect trees, birds and springs.",
    "L4": "Pilgrimage brought people from distant regions together for centuries.",
    "L5": "Along these routes, people shared languages, stories, songs, food, crafts and trade, helping the land feel connected.",
    "L6": "Bodh Gaya became sacred because tradition remembers the Buddha's enlightenment there, and pilgrims carried its importance across countries.",
    "L7": "One place can matter to several traditions. Mount Kailash is revered by Hindus, Buddhists, Jains and followers of Bon.",
    "L8": "Sacred places also need care today, because pollution and crowding can harm them."
   },
